    "created_at": "2026-09-21T06:30:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-21T06:44:41Z",
    "body": "Eh, I kind of doubt browsers want to invest much time here, especially with potential compat risk. And implementing a full XML parser, but I guess at the byte level instead of the character level so that you can run it during the early stages before decoding, seems like a big project?\n\n(If browsers did want to make compat-affecting changes here... I wonder how many XML documents browsers ever encounter with non-UTF charsets? Maybe it's low enough that scanning for the encoding declaration could be dropped completely, for XML.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
